{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"567693a5-c345-4ec6-9f7c-03452eb1fcba","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Investigation \u0026 Root Cause\n\nChecking [Library/Logs/nightly-review.err](file:///tmp/h-Pvx0Z8/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err) and [launchctl-print.txt](file:///tmp/h-Pvx0Z8/launchctl-print.txt) revealed why nothing was ever reported:\n\n1. **Authentication Failure in Claude**:\n   The `claude` command failed on execution, outputting `Not logged in · Please run /login` and returning exit code `1`.\n2. **Fatal Zsh Shell Error Preventing Notification**:\n   In Zsh, `status` is a built-in read-only variable aliased to `$?`. Attempting to assign `status=$?` at line 19 of [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-Pvx0Z8/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L19) produced:\n   ```\n   read-only variable: status\n   ```\n   This caused the shell script to abort execution immediately at line 19. The subsequent error-handling block that invokes [bin/notify.sh](file:///tmp/h-Pvx0Z8/bin/notify.sh) to send failure notices was never reached.\n\n---\n\n### Fix Applied\n\n- In [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-Pvx0Z8/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24), replaced the read-only variable `status` with `exit_code` so that failed runs proceed to the error-handling block and invoke `notify.sh`.\n- Detailed the analysis and findings in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-Pvx0Z8/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":98.749073,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":158181,"output_tokens":2528,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":365074,"total_tokens":160709}}}
